  "notes": "'?' (y ~1640) is the E-W street from the Quebec/Warsaw junction east past Ross, Kuhlman, Riolen and Wessels; printed only as 'AVENUE' (east, near x 8900); its westward continuation west of Quebec (y ~1770, Seton T) is also unnamed in my reading, and is recorded as the same '?' street. The two '?' T's on West Liberty Street (x 5287, x 5665) are streets running north off the plate top (stubs cut by the plate edge; the eastern one's label begins 'K'). 'Mayfield Avenue' east of Ross is printed only 'AVENUE'; taken as Mayfield (same line as MAYFIELD west of Ross). Glenway Avenue (y ~3500-3850) is printed only 'AVENUE' in this strip; name from the plate description, it joins Warsaw at Enright (east of there the plate prints WARSAW). Liberty west of Quebec printed 'STREET', east 'W. LIBERTY ST.'. Hamilton Avenue (x ~5525, y 5340-5830) and Hazard Street (x ~6125) are printed '(VACATED)' and are not recorded. 'GLEN GROVE', 'G.F. MEYER'S', 'KUHLMAN'S', 'CYNTHIA TERRY'S', 'ELIZ. McCABE'S', 'SEVERS' spaced lettering are subdivision names; the grey bands along them are boundaries, not streets. Middle lines drawn along Glenway, Laclede, the '?' street and Seton were used as centrelines."
